120
00:22:47.880 --> 00:23:00.770
Brendan Miller (Applied Social Media Lab at the Berkman Klein Center for Internet & Society): I'm going to create a new identifier for myself every time I connect with another person, whether we're in the same trust community or not. So this is intended to make things non-correlatable by default.

121
00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:23.399
Brendan Miller (Applied Social Media Lab at the Berkman Klein Center for Internet & Society): unlinkable. And, and so then you have this choice about what to disclose. So the R card says, this is what I want this human to know. Our persona credential is another layer on top of that, which says, I'm going to actually give you a stable identifier to link to this transaction. I'll give you my public, like, work identifier, if you will.

122
00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:32.910
